  "issue_number": 118,
  "issue_title": "[Bug]: Meta-Programmer source scanner misses `from os import system` \u2014 dangerous-sink calls bypass the deploy gate (fail-open)",
  "issue_body": "### Component\n\ncoordinator / meta-programmer / beliefs\n\n### Description\n\n`meta_programmer.safety.scan_source` is the defence-in-depth AST taint scan that\nblocks LLM-generated code containing dangerous sinks (`os.system`, `subprocess`,\nsockets, `ctypes`, \u2026) before it is written to disk and hot-loaded. It only\ndetects a dangerous module call in **attribute form** (`os.system(...)`). A call\nto a name pulled in via `from <module> import <sink>` \u2014 e.g.\n\n```python\nfrom os import system\nsystem(\"rm -rf /\")\n```\n\nreaches the `ast.Name` branch, which only checks `_DANGEROUS_BUILTINS` /\n`_REFLECTION_BUILTINS`. `\"system\"` is in neither, and the `ImportFrom` only\nproduces a **medium** `dangerous_import` finding. Since `is_dangerous()` (and the\ndeploy gate in `service.py`) block **only high-severity** findings, the code is\nclassified **not dangerous** and proceeds to staging \u2192 Kernel (which sees only a\n500-char preview) \u2192 sandbox \u2192 deploy/hot-load. This is a fail-open in the safety\nlayer: an arbitrary-command-execution sink the scanner exists to block sails\nthrough.\n\n#### Root cause (code)\n\n`meta-programmer/src/meta_programmer/safety.py`, `scan_source`:\n\n```python\n        if isinstance(node, ast.Call):\n            fn = node.func\n            if isinstance(fn, ast.Name):\n                if fn.id in _DANGEROUS_BUILTINS:\n                    findings.append(Finding(\"high\", \"dangerous_builtin\", f\"{fn.id}()\"))\n                elif fn.id in _REFLECTION_BUILTINS:\n                    ...\n            elif isinstance(fn, ast.Attribute) and isinstance(fn.value, ast.Name):\n                mod, attr = fn.value.id, fn.attr        # <-- only attribute form (os.system)\n                allowed = _DANGEROUS_MODULES.get(mod, \"MISS\")\n                if allowed != \"MISS\" and (allowed is None or attr in allowed):\n                    findings.append(Finding(\"high\", \"dangerous_call\", f\"{mod}.{attr}()\"))\n        ...\n        elif isinstance(node, ast.ImportFrom):\n            ...\n            if top in _DANGEROUS_MODULES:\n                findings.append(Finding(\"medium\", \"dangerous_import\", ...))   # medium only\n```\n\n```python\ndef is_dangerous(code: str) -> bool:\n    return any(f.severity == \"high\" for f in scan_source(code))\n```\n\nA bare-`Name` call to a `from`-imported sink is never matched, and the import\nitself is only medium \u2014 so nothing high fires.\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n```python\n# from meta-programmer/src:\nfrom meta_programmer.safety import is_dangerous\n\nprint(is_dangerous(\"import os\\nos.system('rm -rf /')\"))        # control\nprint(is_dangerous(\"from os import system\\nsystem('rm -rf /')\"))\nprint(is_dangerous(\"from subprocess import run\\nrun(['ls'])\"))\nprint(is_dangerous(\"from os import popen as p\\np('id')\"))\nprint(is_dangerous(\"from os import *\\nsystem('id')\"))\n```\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nAll of these contain a dangerous sink and must be flagged (blocked):\n\n```\nTrue     # import os / os.system(...)\nTrue     # from os import system / system(...)\nTrue     # from subprocess import run / run(...)\nTrue     # aliased\nTrue     # star import\n```\n\n### Actual Behavior\n\n```shell\nTrue     # import os / os.system(...)   (control \u2014 correctly blocked)\nFalse    # from os import system / system(...)      <-- BYPASS\nFalse    # from subprocess import run / run(...)     <-- BYPASS\nFalse    # from os import popen as p / p('id')       <-- BYPASS\nFalse    # from os import * / system('id')           <-- BYPASS\n```\n\nThe `from`-import form (and `as`-aliased / star variants) is classified\nnot-dangerous and is eligible for deploy + host execution. The existing tests\n(`test_safety.py`) only cover the attribute form (`import os` + `os.system`), so\nthis gap is uncovered.\n\n### Environment\n\n- OS: Windows 10 (platform-independent \u2014 pure stdlib `ast`)\n- Python: 3.11 / 3.12\n- Run mode: any (`python run.py` or Docker)\n- Commit: `dev` @ latest\n\n---\n\n#### Suggested fix (for discussion)\n\nIn `scan_source`, pre-resolve names bound by `from <dangerous_module> import\n<sink> [as alias]` and flag a later bare call to such a name as **high**\n`dangerous_call` (symmetric with the attribute-form check); also flag\n`from <dangerous_module> import *` as high, since it pulls the sinks in wholesale\nand defeats name tracking. Add `test_safety.py` cases for the `from`-import,\naliased, and star forms. Happy to open a PR.\n\n### Pre-submission checks\n\n- [x] I searched existing issues and this is not a duplicate.\n- [x] I am running the latest `dev`.",
